  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133630/assets/b14906ddfde919b60d119d9250ae47ff295d549f757c2a687d6796d09eb661ef.png)\n\nIf the ratio of pentagons to total shapes is $\\frac{4}{\\boxed{}}$ then what is the missing number?",
  "worked_solution": "We count the number of pentagons. We see that there are $4$ pentagons.\n\n We count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $7$ shapes.\n\nHence, the ratio of pentagons to total shapes is$\\frac{4}{7}$\n\nSo the missing number is $7.$",
